      <title>Backrooms and Liminal World Builder Bundle</title>
      <author>Autotroph</author>
      <link>https://humblebundle.com//software/backrooms-and-liminal-world-builder-bundle-software</link>
      <guid isPermaLink="false">3bb9c6234800b6ef129e9b37b2c02557357e22e5</guid>
      <pubDate>Tue, 15 Sep 2026 18:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <description>&lt;div&gt;&lt;img src="https://hb.imgix.net/60ba807a5d2165d796c214ab7e7b34d54835f73c.png?auto=compress,format&amp;h=340&amp;w=1200&amp;s=e09bc6c71b541fe3f2723521f110f07c"&gt;&lt;img src="https://hb.imgix.net/25da09163d5daa175a59ab3c8fc0b8bc026677a9.jpg?auto=compress,format&amp;fit=crop&amp;h=600&amp;w=1200&amp;s=b17cd1b8d50fbcd51061b5b4340d2344"&gt;&lt;h2&gt;Create the next Backrooms!&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;Calling all prospective filmmakers! Create effortlessly with the &lt;em&gt;Backrooms Pro Generator&lt;/em&gt; or the &lt;em&gt;Procedural Backrooms Generator&lt;/em&gt;, with four architectural styles, customizable sliders, and no modeling required! Dress your corridors with 147 hand‑crafted vintage liminal props that make your project feel straight out of the 90s! Give your film the Kane Parsons treatment with his signature VHS/Handycam filter aesthetic. Whether you're chasing internet‑famous liminal‑space content, prototyping a horror game level, or just love the unsettling beauty of empty fluorescent‑lit rooms, this bundle is everything you need to start building your own &lt;em&gt;Backrooms&lt;/em&gt;—no VFX studio required. Plus, your purchase helps support Trees, Water &amp; People!  &lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;span style="color: #ef9741;"&gt;Keys expire. Please redeem your keys before February  28th, 2027. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#0"&gt;Pay $20 to unlock!&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#backroomsprogenerator"&gt;Backrooms Pro Generator&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#proceduralbackroomsgenerator"&gt;Procedural Backrooms Generator&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#vintageliminalprops"&gt;Vintage Liminal Props&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#blender3danimation_discoverthehauntingbeautyofliminalspaces"&gt;Blender 3D Animation: Discover The Haunting Beauty Of Liminal Spaces&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#vhsgenerator"&gt;VHS Generator&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#backroomsbuildingkit"&gt;Backrooms Building Kit&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#backroomsinblenderstepbysteptutorial4h40minplusasteroidscenetutori"&gt;Backrooms In Blender Step By Step Tutorial 4H,40Min (+ Asteroid Scene Tutorial Gratis)&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#poolroomsinblender"&gt;Pool Rooms in Blender&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#backrooms"&gt;The Backrooms&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#poolroomassets"&gt;Poolroom Assets&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#advancedmazegeneratorproforblender"&gt;Advanced Maze Generator Pro for Blender&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#90shandycamfilter"&gt;90S Handycam Filter&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#extralights_superhive"&gt;Extra Lights&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;h2 id="0"&gt;Pay $20 to unlock!&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;h3 id="backroomsprogenerator"&gt;&lt;a id="backroomsprogenerator" href="https://youtu.be/8OzJGRREExg"&gt;Backrooms Pro Generator&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;Backrooms - Pro Generator is a Blender geometry nodes add-on that procedurally builds four distinct Backrooms environments: the Lobby, Poolrooms, Parking Lot, and Hotel styles, each with its own architecture and room layouts. Everything is generated non-destructively, so users adjust room size, corridor width, ceiling height, and lighting through simple slider controls rather than manual modeling. Generated maps export in one click to Godot, Unity, and Unreal Engine as low-poly, game-ready assets. Compatible with Blender 4.5–5.2 and both Cycles and Eevee, it's aimed at game developers and horror-content creators who want fast, fully customizable liminal-space levels without touching a single node themselves.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h3 id="proceduralbackroomsgenerator"&gt;&lt;a id="proceduralbackroomsgenerator" href="https://youtu.be/vLakbZvk15o"&gt;Procedural Backrooms Generator&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;This modifier-based setup turns the classic Backrooms look into a fully procedural Blender workflow. Office lighting, wallpapered walls, and yellow, damp carpet (or a clean variant) are all controlled through sliders, letting users extrude, stretch, and reshape corridors into custom mazes. Lighting runs on optimized area lamps rather than large emissive planes, keeping render times fast in both Eevee and Cycles, and imperfections are pulled from real office-wear textures instead of generic noise. Six objects are Asset Browser-ready, with three functioning as procedural generators capable of near-endless combinations. Includes a full instructional video.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h3 id="vintageliminalprops"&gt;&lt;a id="vintageliminalprops" href="https://youtu.be/wSpxeoguWlM"&gt;Vintage Liminal Props&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;A collection of 147 hand-modeled, hand-textured Blender assets capturing the late-1980s/early-90s aesthetic that defines most liminal-space scenes, created as a companion to Procedural Backrooms Generator. Assets span five categories: Electronics (retro computers, CRTs, cassette tapes, surveillance gear), Office furniture, Furniture (seating, cabinets, tables, shelving), Decor (lamps, framed art, clocks), and Outdoor (small houses, garages, fences, building parts). Each object uses optimized, clean topology with advanced shaders for realistic light interaction rather than relying on high poly counts. The whole library is organized and categorized for Blender's Asset Browser, with a detailed installation video walking through setup.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h3 id="blender3danimation_discoverthehauntingbeautyofliminalspaces"&gt;&lt;a id="blender3danimation_discoverthehauntingbeautyofliminalspaces" href="https://youtu.be/2VekwgthLtw"&gt;Blender 3D Animation: Discover The Haunting Beauty Of Liminal Spaces&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;A beginner-focused video course by Harry Helps, a professional 3D artist and former studio director at an architectural visualization firm, teaching students to model and animate a liminal space from scratch. Across 14 lessons and roughly 3 hours of instruction (plus two bonus "Blender Crash Course" lessons for absolute newcomers), students build a flooded corridor, set up soft volumetric lighting, texture tile and water surfaces, unwrap UVs, composite for a nostalgic low-fidelity look, and animate a subtly looping water texture. Includes a completed Blender 3.6.2 project file, final MP4/GIF renders for reference, and a keyboard-shortcut cheat sheet.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h3 id="vhsgenerator"&gt;&lt;a id="vhsgenerator" href="https://youtu.be/HeGL2Lb99vw"&gt;VHS Generator&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;VHS Generator is a Blender add-on that recreates authentic analog video artifacts directly inside the Compositor using a high-performance node system. It ships with three specialized camera modes: Classic VHS, Security Camera/CCTV, and 90s Camcorder, each with five presets ranging from subtle to heavily "grungy," for 15 total looks. Adjustable parameters cover scanlines, interlacing, lens curvature, animated static grain, digital noise, tracking-band distortion, RGB shift/chromatic aberration, color balance (lift/gamma/gain), and posterization. It's a solid fit for anyone building retro, horror, or liminal-space footage that needs a convincing degraded-tape aesthetic.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h3 id="backroomsbuildingkit"&gt;&lt;a id="backroomsbuildingkit"&gt;Backrooms Building Kit&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;img src="https://hb.imgix.net/cd74e878a93b546852b287766760ba9d6354b2e6.jpg?auto=compress,format&amp;fit=clip&amp;h=350&amp;w=600&amp;s=f847cd0bc046b86b32e6e9afd16dcf67"&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;A modular Backrooms kit is built for hand-assembling custom maze layouts in Blender. It includes precisely modeled wall segments, furniture, and props alongside smart materials for ceiling, wallpaper, and floor surfaces, meaning textures automatically adapt as pieces are scaled, extruded, or moved without stretching or breaking. Also bundled are custom analog/VHS-style overlays for giving renders a distorted, degraded look straight out of the compositor. An included video walks through the full building process so users can start assembling their own Backrooms scenes right away.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h3 id="backroomsinblenderstepbysteptutorial4h40minplusasteroidscenetutori"&gt;&lt;a id="backroomsinblenderstepbysteptutorial4h40minplusasteroidscenetutori" href="https://youtu.be/3iKXHumiIVo"&gt;Backrooms In Blender Step By Step Tutorial 4H,40Min (+ Asteroid Scene Tutorial Gratis)&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;A comprehensive 4-hour-40-minute video tutorial by Šime Bugarija covering the full process of building a Backrooms scene in Blender, from modeling rooms, walls, and mazes through materials, ventilation, smoke detectors, and pipes, to compositing mist and camera imperfections, adding graffiti and dirt, animating a camera in two different ways, importing a Mixamo creature, and finishing with After Effects (or Blender) post-processing including VHS overlays and sound design. English audio with subtitles, 2K resolution, and full .blend/project files included. Buyers also get a bonus tutorial on creating an Asteroid Scene.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h3 id="poolroomsinblender"&gt;&lt;a id="poolroomsinblender" href="https://youtu.be/_8SnKGu6Wa8"&gt;Pool Rooms in Blender&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;Šime Bugarija's follow-up to his popular Backrooms tutorial, this 4+ hour, 26-chapter course walks through building a Poolrooms environment from the ground up, modeling non-destructive mazes of varying shapes, rounded stairs, and windows. Lighting both open daylight spaces and closed interiors. Creating and animating realistic ocean-modifier water with caustics that don't tank render times. Texturing carpet, tile, chrome, and glass. Finishing with realistic camera movement and an authentic VHS-style post-processing pass. English audio with subtitles, 2K resolution, full .blend and project files included.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h3 id="backrooms"&gt;&lt;a id="backrooms" href="https://youtu.be/SCoRxIDeMcs"&gt;The Backrooms&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;A simple, modular Backrooms interior model by Dusan Lamos, built to closely match the original viral Backrooms photograph. Its wall textures were pulled directly from a hi-res version of that source image. Textures are supplied at 4K resolution for walls and 2K for smaller assets, with preview renders done in Cycles. The package includes a .blend file with textures packed in, plus separate .fbx and .obj exports and a standalone .rar archive of just the texture files, making it straightforward to bring into other engines or pipelines&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h3 id="poolroomassets"&gt;&lt;a id="poolroomassets" href="https://youtu.be/rJUOTrPp8Ts"&gt;Poolroom Assets&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;Poolroom Assets is a lightweight, all-in-one prop pack for building "Poolrooms"-style liminal environments without setting everything up from scratch. It includes a curated set of poolroom-specific models, two water-slide geometry-node setups (one open, one closed), a tile texture and a water texture, a ready-to-use ocean modifier for animated water, poolroom-style lights, and a wave-deform geometry node that makes floating objects bob naturally on the water's surface. It's a fast starting point for anyone producing the endless-tiled-void aesthetic that's popular in pool room and dreamcore-style videos.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h3 id="advancedmazegeneratorproforblender"&gt;&lt;a id="advancedmazegeneratorproforblender"&gt;Advanced Maze Generator Pro for Blender&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;img src="https://hb.imgix.net/ee9edb2d1043ac09b55daf61e09c7b08dd7a2115.jpg?auto=compress,format&amp;fit=clip&amp;h=350&amp;w=600&amp;s=798ab525479351801e443b4cf0699e13"&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;A professional-grade maze creation add-on offering more than 20 generation algorithms (Recursive Backtracking, Kruskal's, Prim's, Wilson's, Eller's, Growing Tree, and more) applied across a wide range of maze shapes: rectangles, circles, hexagons, stars, spirals, fractals, and custom outlines. Professional controls cover complexity tuning, symmetry, room generation, central-path styling, loop control, and weighted/heat-map-based generation, plus visual options for wall/floor styles, solution-path visualization, and start/end markers. Supports batch generation, JSON import/export, and performance monitoring. Useful for game level design, architectural layouts, education, and procedural art.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h3 id="90shandycamfilter"&gt;&lt;a id="90shandycamfilter" href="https://youtu.be/KPWLbERFid0"&gt;90S Handycam Filter&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;A one-click compositor filter that transforms Blender renders into authentic 90s camcorder or dreamcore-style footage. It layers soft focus, chromatic aberration, CCD bloom, and pixelated compression artifacts together with dynamic tape noise and signal jitter for organic, retro movement, all controlled from within the Render Properties panel. Four one-click presets: Homevideo, Dreamcore, 80s TV, and Surveillance, cover common looks without manual tweaking.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h3 id="extralights_superhive"&gt;&lt;a id="extralights_superhive"&gt;Extra Lights&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;img src="https://hb.imgix.net/40b79c1194d4a264055fb9ea2b3708335d37206e.jpg?auto=compress,format&amp;fit=clip&amp;h=350&amp;w=600&amp;s=5eb3f0e07571f817c416e75e2dfed696"&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;Extra Lights adds over 60 physically based light presets to Blender's Add menu, modeled on real-world fixtures and organized by type and strength — including 30+ point/spot/area/sun presets and 30+ IES presets with believable real-world beam patterns. Each light's brightness is set in lumens rather than watts, with accurate Kelvin color temperatures so mixed light sources look natural together, and an included lumens-conversion node group works with any Cycles light type. Sun presets auto-link to a matching sky and position correctly above the camera.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</description>
      <category>software</category>
      <category>Backrooms and Liminal World Builder Bundle</category>
      <category>13 items</category>
      <category>$175 Value</category>
    </item>
