eractiveterminalla"&gt;Red Hat Certified Specialist in Security: Linux with Interactive Terminal Labs&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#susecertifiedadministratorinsuselinuxenterpriseserver16withpractic"&gt;SUSE Certified Administrator in SUSE Linux Enterprise Server 16 with Practice Exam&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#linuxfoundationcertifiedsystemadministratorlfcswithpracticeexam"&gt;Linux Foundation Certified System Administrator (LFCS) with Practice Exam&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#linuxfoundationcertifieditassociatelfcawithpracticeexam"&gt;Linux Foundation Certified IT Associate (LFCA) with Practice Exam&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#certifiedkubernetessecurityspecialistckswithpracticeexam"&gt;Certified Kubernetes Security Specialist (CKS) with Practice Exam&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#certifiedkubernetesadministratorckawithpracticeexam"&gt;Certified Kubernetes Administrator (CKA) with Practice Exam&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#rhcsa_redhatcertifiedsystemadministrator20with10practiceexams"&gt;RHCSA: Red Hat Certified System Administrator 2.0 with 10 Practice Exams&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#rhce_redhatcertifiedengineer20with10practiceexams"&gt;RHCE: Red Hat Certified Engineer 2.0 with 10 Practice Exams&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#completelinuxessentialscertificatev16with10practiceexams"&gt;The Complete Linux Essentials Certificate V1.6 with 10 Practice Exams&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#klcp_kalilinuxcertifiedprofessional_10practiceexams"&gt;OffSec Kali Linux Certified Professional (KLCP) Certification with 10 Practice Exams&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#lpic-1certification_linuxadministratorwith10practiceexams"&gt;LPIC-1 Certification: Linux Administrator with 10 Practice Exams&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#lpic-2certification_linuxengineerwith10practiceexams"&gt;LPIC-2 Certification: Linux Engineer with 10 Practice Exams  &lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#expertlpic-3securitycertificationwith10practiceexams"&gt;EXPERT LPIC-3 Security Certification with 10 Practice Exams  &lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#advancedlinuxandbashscriptingforethicalhacking"&gt;Advanced Linux and Bash Scripting for Ethical Hacking&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#linuxmasteryforethicalhacking_packagemanagementpermissionsandtextp"&gt;Linux Mastery for Ethical Hacking: Package Management, Permissions, and Text Processing&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#hands-onandroidhackinglabs_decompilingcodepatternsvulnerabilities"&gt;Hands-on Android Hacking Labs: Decompiling, Code Patterns, Vulnerabilities&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#linuxfundamentalsforethicalhacking_thecompletejourney"&gt;Linux Fundamentals for Ethical Hacking&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#ethicalhackingandpenetrationtestingguide"&gt;Ethical Hacking and Penetration Testing&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#advancedandroidhacking_deepdiveintofridareverseengineeringandappma"&gt;Advanced Android Hacking: Deep Dive into Frida, Reverse Engineering, and App Manipulation&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#microsoftpowershellfundamentalswithazureft10practiceexams"&gt;Microsoft PowerShell Fundamentals with Azure ft 10 Practice Exams&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#automatingdatabaseworkflowswithn8nandsqlfirst-timeexclusivehumbleb"&gt;Automating Database Workflows with n8n &amp; SQL&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#webapplicationsecurity"&gt;Web Application Security&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#pyspark_builddataframeswithpythonapachesparkandsql"&gt;PySpark - Build Dataframes with Python, Apache, Spark and SQL&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#dataprotectionandencryption"&gt;Data Protection and Encryption&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#pythonandsqlitebootcamp_learntobuilddatabases"&gt;Python and SQLite Bootcamp - Learn to Build Databases&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#linuxandunixcommandlinebasicsforbashzshellandubuntu"&gt;Linux and Unix Command Line Basics for Bash, Z Shell and Ubuntu&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#beginnersandroidhacking_practicallabsetupandtheoreticalfoundations"&gt;Beginners Android Hacking: Practical Lab Setup and Theoretical Foundations&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#pythonprogrammingfundamentalsvideoseries"&gt;Python Programming Fundamentals Video Series&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#windowsterminalprofiles_customizationandefficiencyunleashed"&gt;Windows Terminal Profiles: Customization and Efficiency Unleashed&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#mobilesecurityvanguard-bestpracticesandstrategieswithpracticeexam"&gt;Mobile Security Vanguard - Best Practices and Strategies with Practice Exam&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#cloudsecurityandriskmanagement"&gt;Cloud Security and Risk Management&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#incidentresponseandthreathunting"&gt;Incident Response and Threat Hunting&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;h2 id="0"&gt;Pay $5 to unlock!&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;h3 id="windowsterminal101_astep-by-stepguideforbeginners"&gt;&lt;a id="windowsterminal101_astep-by-stepguideforbeginners" href="https://youtu.be/hMwXlyC1qso"&gt;Windows Terminal 101: A Step-by-Step Guide for Beginners&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;img src="https://hb.imgix.net/32b9c8f39e52dd5c3a22628ae44eeb42a32dd811.jpg?auto=compress,format&amp;fit=clip&amp;h=350&amp;w=600&amp;s=e23bb664ab4f92cd7f326d0064ef64ee"&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;Windows Terminal replaced the old console window, and it is worth setting up properly.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Installation through appearance settings, in order.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;► Installing Windows Terminal.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;► Startup settings and running as administrator.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;► Interaction settings.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;► Appearance, color schemes, and tabs.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;► Rendering options and actions.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Everything here is a setting you can change in a minute once you know where it lives.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;✅ Lifetime access to all modules and source files.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Install it and make it yours.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h2 id="bt15"&gt;Pay $15 or more to also unlock!&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;h3 id="windowsconfigurationwizard-unlockingsystemmasterywithpracticeexam"&gt;&lt;a id="windowsconfigurationwizard-unlockingsystemmasterywithpracticeexam" href="https://youtu.be/hMwXlyC1qso"&gt;Windows Configuration Wizard - Unlocking System Mastery with Practice Exam&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;img src="https://hb.imgix.net/befcc11efbcd3369b1c7dc0d802263d816c7e46c.jpg?auto=compress,format&amp;fit=clip&amp;h=350&amp;w=600&amp;s=24e896f826d3f66a46f96e65da69f0d7"&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;Windows Configuration Designer turns repeated setup steps into a provisioning package you apply once.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Interface first, then basic packages, then advanced customization.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;► Benefits and use cases for provisioning.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;► Installing WCD and finding your way around.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;► Testing safely in virtual machines.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;► Building basic provisioning packages.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;► Advanced provisioning and customization.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Configuring 40 machines by hand is a choice, and this shows the alternative.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;✅ Lifetime access to all modules and source files.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;✅ Practice exam with unlimited attempts.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Build one package and deploy it everywhere.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h2 id="bt30"&gt;Pay $30 or more to also unlock!&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;h3 id="comptialinuxplusxk0-006withpracticeexam"&gt;&lt;a id="comptialinuxplusxk0-006withpracticeexam" href="https://youtu.be/hMwXlyC1qso"&gt;CompTIA Linux+ (XK0-006) with Practice Exam&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;img src="https://hb.imgix.net/0b282aac8f7a4785c394bb399c31636cd028d762.jpg?auto=compress,format&amp;fit=clip&amp;h=350&amp;w=600&amp;s=ee58e3d990017eaee56b0c4d23c4dfca"&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;Linux+ is vendor neutral, so it checks whether you can run a Linux system without leaning on one distribution's habits.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The XK0-006 objectives are broad, and this covers the ground an admin works across day to day.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;► Command line work and file system handling.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;► Users, permissions, and access control.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;► Networking, storage, and service configuration.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;► Scripting, containers, and troubleshooting.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Work through the sections in order and the objective list starts looking familiar instead of intimidating.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;✅ Lifetime access to all modules and source files.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;✅ Practice exam with unlimited attempts.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Get comfortable with the fundamentals, then go sit the exam.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h3 id="redhatcertifiedspecialistinsecurity_linuxwithinteractiveterminalla"&gt;&lt;a id="redhatcertifiedspecialistinsecurity_linuxwithinteractiveterminalla" href="https://youtu.be/hMwXlyC1qso"&gt;Red Hat Certified Specialist in Security: Linux with Interactive Terminal Labs&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;img src="https://hb.imgix.net/54640f463b802900df7b4f54a63fd9f7aa112cfd.jpg?auto=compress,format&amp;fit=clip&amp;h=350&amp;w=600&amp;s=279e8227b78b5459e338ce29583b929a"&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;Securing RHEL is hands on work, not a policy document you file away.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The material follows the exam objectives so you know what the graders look for.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;► SELinux contexts, policy, and enforcement modes.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;► Auditing, logging, and system integrity checks.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;► Encryption for data at rest and in transit.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;► Identity, authentication, and access control.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Security specialists get called first when something looks wrong, and this is the groundwork for being useful in that moment.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;✅ Lifetime access to all modules and source files.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;✅ Interactive terminal labs to test your skills.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Start hardening, then get the credential to prove it.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h3 id="susecertifiedadministratorinsuselinuxenterpriseserver16withpractic"&gt;&lt;a id="susecertifiedadministratorinsuselinuxenterpriseserver16withpractic" href="https://youtu.be/hMwXlyC1qso"&gt;SUSE Certified Administrator in SUSE Linux Enterprise Server 16 with Practice Exam&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;img src="https://hb.imgix.net/c7f555656fc38e53f708ec6a701f631177a57809.jpg?auto=compress,format&amp;fit=clip&amp;h=350&amp;w=600&amp;s=94404bddac9d55ecb5e22da4bef20261"&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;SLES runs in plenty of enterprise racks, and it has its own tooling worth learning properly.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Everything here maps to the administrator level tasks the certification tests.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;► Installation, updates, and zypper package handling.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;► systemd services, storage, and file systems.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;► Users, permissions, and firewall configuration.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;► Shell work and routine troubleshooting.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;If your shop runs SUSE, knowing it specifically puts you ahead of admins who only know Ubuntu.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;✅ Lifetime access to all modules and source files.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;✅ Practice exam with unlimited attempts.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Learn the SUSE way and add the certification to your record.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h3 id="linuxfoundationcertifiedsystemadministratorlfcswithpracticeexam"&gt;&lt;a id="linuxfoundationcertifiedsystemadministratorlfcswithpracticeexam" href="https://youtu.be/hMwXlyC1qso"&gt;Linux Foundation Certified System Administrator (LFCS) with Practice Exam&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;img src="https://hb.imgix.net/dd1d34a55a33176d5a86aab5199f6cd11ebb914c.jpg?auto=compress,format&amp;fit=clip&amp;h=350&amp;w=600&amp;s=1d6c3e83b09ef6ed8d734d3d412f311c"&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;The LFCS is a performance based exam, which means you type commands rather than pick answers.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Practice matters more than memorizing here, and that shapes how this is put together.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;► Command operations and shell scripting.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;► Users, groups, and file permissions.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;► Storage, volumes, and file systems.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;► Networking, services, and system logs.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Sysadmin work rewards people who can fix a system under time pressure, and that is what this exam measures.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;✅ Lifetime access to all modules and source files.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;✅ Practice exam with unlimited attempts.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Build the command line habits the LFCS asks for.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h3 id="linuxfoundationcertifieditassociatelfcawithpracticeexam"&gt;&lt;a id="linuxfoundationcertifieditassociatelfcawithpracticeexam" href="https://youtu.be/hMwXlyC1qso"&gt;Linux Foundation Certified IT Associate (LFCA) with Practice Exam&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;img src="https://hb.imgix.net/e8356b45f55cb3a95009be49e57c770ed73140d8.jpg?auto=compress,format&amp;fit=clip&amp;h=350&amp;w=600&amp;s=047a4fa9df4d8d0bf791ce0f22ddd4b4"&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;LFCA is the entry point, aimed at people starting an IT career rather than already in one.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Expect breadth over depth, since the exam covers a bit of everything an IT associate touches.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;► IT basics, hardware, and operating systems.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;► Linux fundamentals and the command line.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;► Networking, security, and cloud concepts.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;► Support workflows and troubleshooting.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;A first certification gives recruiters something concrete to look at when you have no job history yet.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;✅ Lifetime access to all modules and source files.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;✅ Practice exam with unlimited attempts.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Take the first step into IT with the LFCA.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h3 id="certifiedkubernetessecurityspecialistckswithpracticeexam"&gt;&lt;a id="certifiedkubernetessecurityspecialistckswithpracticeexam" href="https://youtu.be/hMwXlyC1qso"&gt;Certified Kubernetes Security Specialist (CKS) with Practice Exam&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;img src="https://hb.imgix.net/4d10bfd64f869900faf74d0ca633618825ec39ef.jpg?auto=compress,format&amp;fit=clip&amp;h=350&amp;w=600&amp;s=2496c8043aae29ab24168bc5b7b0daae"&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;CKS assumes you already hold a current CKA, so it starts where cluster administration leaves off.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Like the other Kubernetes exams, it is performance based, and the material stays on the tasks rather than the theory.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;► Cluster setup, hardening, and network policies.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;► Supply chain security for images and manifests.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;► Minimizing microservice vulnerabilities and RBAC scope.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;► Runtime security, monitoring, and audit logging.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Security work on a cluster tends to land on whoever already knows how the cluster runs, and this is the layer that follows.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;✅ Lifetime access to all modules and source files.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;✅ Graded practice exam with unlimited attempts.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Harden what you already know how to build.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h3 id="certifiedkubernetesadministratorckawithpracticeexam"&gt;&lt;a id="certifiedkubernetesadministratorckawithpracticeexam" href="https://youtu.be/hMwXlyC1qso"&gt;Certified Kubernetes Administrator (CKA) with Practice Exam&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;img src="https://hb.imgix.net/b9d5b057f35964dbd290ca41fcc7a325adc304b5.jpg?auto=compress,format&amp;fit=clip&amp;h=350&amp;w=600&amp;s=0c13a85a62615b39bc99c4fd4a0b6039"&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;Running a cluster is a different job from deploying to one, and CKA tests the first.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The exam is entirely hands on, so the material keeps you in the terminal.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;► Cluster architecture, installation, and upgrades.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;► Workloads, scheduling, and node management.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;► Services, networking, and cluster DNS.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;► Storage, RBAC, and troubleshooting failures.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Cluster administrators are the people who get paged, and knowing the recovery paths is what makes that survivable.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;✅ Lifetime access to all modules and source files.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;✅ Practice exam with unlimited attempts.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Take the cluster apart, put it back, then pass the CKA.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h3 id="rhcsa_redhatcertifiedsystemadministrator20with10practiceexams"&gt;&lt;a id="rhcsa_redhatcertifiedsystemadministrator20with10practiceexams" href="https://youtu.be/hMwXlyC1qso"&gt;RHCSA: Red Hat Certified System Administrator 2.0 with 10 Practice Exams&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;img src="https://hb.imgix.net/af76889910dc24f08fb7cb26c0b3e2aac2f71dbf.jpg?auto=compress,format&amp;fit=clip&amp;h=350&amp;w=600&amp;s=37792bbed879ca9afad99d1ccb4484ab"&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;RHCSA is graded on tasks you complete, so the material follows the commands rather than the theory.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;► Command line, permissions, and system documentation.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;► DNF and Flatpak software management.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;► Shell scripting and systemd service management.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;► Storage, LVM, file systems, and persistent mounts.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;► Boot recovery, including root password resets.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;► Networking, firewalld, SELinux, and container basics.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Recovering a system through rd.break is the kind of task you want to have done before exam day, not during it.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;✅ Lifetime access to all modules and source files.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;✅ Practice exam with unlimited attempts.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Get hands on with RHEL and earn the RHCSA.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h3 id="rhce_redhatcertifiedengineer20with10practiceexams"&gt;&lt;a id="rhce_redhatcertifiedengineer20with10practiceexams" href="https://youtu.be/hMwXlyC1qso"&gt;RHCE: Red Hat Certified Engineer 2.0 with 10 Practice Exams&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;img src="https://hb.imgix.net/32f7769507745a8a9718df0219a2b96f8faa2bf9.jpg?auto=compress,format&amp;fit=clip&amp;h=350&amp;w=600&amp;s=8e7bdd922416251f5fd67ab855fec7bb"&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;RHCE is an Ansible exam. If you hold the RHCSA, this is the automation layer on top of it.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Components come first, then playbooks, then automating the RHCSA tasks you already know.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;► Inventories, modules, variables, facts, and loops.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;► Conditionals, plays, and task failure handling.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;► Roles and content collections in playbooks.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;► Control node and managed node setup with SSH keys.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;► Automation content navigator for running playbooks.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;► Templates and Ansible Vault for sensitive data.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Converting a shell script into a playbook is covered directly, which is how most people arrive at Ansible.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;✅ Lifetime access to all modules and source files.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;✅ Practice exam with unlimited attempts.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Automate the work you are already doing by hand.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h3 id="completelinuxessentialscertificatev16with10practiceexams"&gt;&lt;a id="completelinuxessentialscertificatev16with10practiceexams" href="https://youtu.be/hMwXlyC1qso"&gt;The Complete Linux Essentials Certificate V1.6 with 10 Practice Exams&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;img src="https://hb.imgix.net/95e0a7c4d7a548d57d092375691fd3463b1622ca.jpg?auto=compress,format&amp;fit=clip&amp;h=350&amp;w=600&amp;s=1ffaa19ec1568179b63eada968ae0904"&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;Linux Essentials assumes nothing, which makes it the right starting point if you are new to all of it.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;5 domains and more than 60 lectures, running from Linux history to file permissions.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;► Distribution families, licensing, and open source communities.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;► Linux in cloud, mobile, and embedded systems.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;► Shell basics, man pages, and file navigation.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;► tar, compression, pipes, grep, sort, cut, and wc.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;► Shell scripts with variables, arguments, and for loops.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;► Users, groups, sudo, chmod, chown, and symbolic links.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Every later Linux certification builds on this material, so time spent here pays off twice.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;✅ Lifetime access to all modules and source files.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;✅ Practice exam with unlimited attempts.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Begin at the first lecture and work through.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h3 id="klcp_kalilinuxcertifiedprofessional_10practiceexams"&gt;&lt;a id="klcp_kalilinuxcertifiedprofessional_10practiceexams" href="https://youtu.be/hMwXlyC1qso"&gt;OffSec Kali Linux Certified Professional (KLCP) Certification with 10 Practice Exams&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;img src="https://hb.imgix.net/e419ce09a369f553673ad7d6d83712012f42fdb1.jpg?auto=compress,format&amp;fit=clip&amp;h=350&amp;w=600&amp;s=f0c1c1a50860f4f1df51ed7c426ded5b"&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;KLCP covers Kali itself: installing it, securing it, and rebuilding it to suit your work.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;From verifying the ISO to running a penetration test with the tools it ships.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;► Downloading, verifying, and booting Kali Linux.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;► Installs on disk, encrypted, unattended, and ARM.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;► Configuring network, users, services, PostgreSQL, and Apache.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;► APT, Debian package management, and recompiling packages.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;► Security policy, firewalls, log monitoring, and change detection.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;► Custom live ISO builds with persistence.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;► Vulnerability assessment, penetration tests, and attack types.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Filing a proper bug report is in here too, which says something about what the certification values.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;✅ Lifetime access to all modules and source files.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;✅ Practice exam with unlimited attempts.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Learn the distribution behind the tools.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h3 id="lpic-1certification_linuxadministratorwith10practiceexams"&gt;&lt;a id="lpic-1certification_linuxadministratorwith10practiceexams" href="https://youtu.be/hMwXlyC1qso"&gt;LPIC-1 Certification: Linux Administrator with 10 Practice Exams&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;img src="https://hb.imgix.net/e9b38c9f17591c32df9a87d4c1750a10642c6800.jpg?auto=compress,format&amp;fit=clip&amp;h=350&amp;w=600&amp;s=9d1181743a815291cad139cba53fc7b9"&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;LPIC-1 covers exams 101 and 102, and it is distribution neutral by design.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The course, following the objective numbering so you can track progress against the official list.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;► Hardware, kernel modules, boot process, and system state.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;► Disk layout, GRUB2, apt, rpm, and shared libraries.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;► Shell environment, quoting, history, and process management.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;► Text processing with grep, find, xargs, and regular expressions.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;► Permissions, links, and the Filesystem Hierarchy Standard.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;► X11, users and groups, cron, logging, printing, and networking.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Both exam halves sit in one place, which saves hunting for 102 material separately.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;✅ Lifetime access to all modules and source files.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;✅ Practice exam with unlimited attempts.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Sit 101 and 102 with the same preparation behind you.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h3 id="lpic-2certification_linuxengineerwith10practiceexams"&gt;&lt;a id="lpic-2certification_linuxengineerwith10practiceexams" href="https://youtu.be/hMwXlyC1qso"&gt;LPIC-2 Certification: Linux Engineer with 10 Practice Exams  &lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;img src="https://hb.imgix.net/a03405461a67d19ae7144e8274108c67995c41df.jpg?auto=compress,format&amp;fit=clip&amp;h=350&amp;w=600&amp;s=165e5446b724e13e46be6e87ffc9743c"&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;LPIC-2 moves past administration into engineering: kernels, capacity, and the services a network runs on.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The course follow the 201 and 202 objectives directly.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;► Capacity planning across CPU, memory, disk, and network.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;► Kernel compilation, boot sequence, and system recovery.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;► RAID, LVM, and filesystem maintenance.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;► DNS with BIND 9, zones, TSIG, and DNSSEC.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;► Apache, Nginx, and Squid, including HTTPS hardening.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;► Samba, NFS, DHCP, LDAP, Postfix, SSH, and OpenVPN.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Diagnosing an I/O bottleneck and configuring a reverse proxy are both engineer level tasks, and both are here.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;✅ Lifetime access to all modules and source files.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;✅ Practice exam with unlimited attempts.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Step up from administrator to engineer.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h3 id="expertlpic-3securitycertificationwith10practiceexams"&gt;&lt;a id="expertlpic-3securitycertificationwith10practiceexams" href="https://youtu.be/hMwXlyC1qso"&gt;EXPERT LPIC-3 Security Certification with 10 Practice Exams  &lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;img src="https://hb.imgix.net/a11cb4257ea110ee7f4b5e43cc8e43f83f92312c.jpg?auto=compress,format&amp;fit=clip&amp;h=350&amp;w=600&amp;s=bbaeb87ce321f0b7ad0ba09ea85a653d"&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;LPIC-3 sits at the top of the LPI track, and the depth reflects that.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Samba and identity management take up the first half, cryptography and network defense the second.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;► Samba architecture, shares, permissions, and VFS modules.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;► Active Directory domains and Windows client management.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;► Winbind, SSSD, PAM, and Kerberos tickets.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;► FreeIPA deployment, replication, and AD trusts.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;► OpenSSL, LUKS, encrypted filesystems, and NFSv4 with Kerberos.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;► SELinux, AppArmor, iptables, IDS, and OpenVPN labs.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Cross realm trusts and DNSSEC are the kind of topics that separate an expert level exam from a professional one.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;✅ Lifetime access to all modules and source files.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;✅ Practice exam with unlimited attempts.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Take on the highest tier of the LPI track.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h3 id="advancedlinuxandbashscriptingforethicalhacking"&gt;&lt;a id="advancedlinuxandbashscriptingforethicalhacking" href="https://youtu.be/hMwXlyC1qso"&gt;Advanced Linux and Bash Scripting for Ethical Hacking&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;img src="https://hb.imgix.net/2338552bb0513b2848b8b59b4bd4c814fabf414b.jpg?auto=compress,format&amp;fit=clip&amp;h=350&amp;w=600&amp;s=2acdc9453c50e84dd85ccf8f819f20c6"&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;Once the basic commands stop slowing you down, the next step is automating what you keep repeating.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;This picks up at networking commands and ends with scripts that take arguments.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;► Networking commands and browsing from the terminal.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;► Reverse shells and bind shells, explained plainly.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;► Process management and tracking open files with lsof.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;► Bash scripting with conditions, loops, and arguments.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Scripting is what separates someone who runs tools from someone who chains them together.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;✅ Lifetime access to all modules and source files.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Open a terminal and start writing your own.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h3 id="linuxmasteryforethicalhacking_packagemanagementpermissionsandtextp"&gt;&lt;a id="linuxmasteryforethicalhacking_packagemanagementpermissionsandtextp" href="https://youtu.be/hMwXlyC1qso"&gt;Linux Mastery for Ethical Hacking: Package Management, Permissions, and Text Processing&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;img src="https://hb.imgix.net/eedebc7931d42b856d21890bdecc5344060f7590.jpg?auto=compress,format&amp;fit=clip&amp;h=350&amp;w=600&amp;s=608ab9113289367826c41bc97907d730"&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;Permissions and text processing come up in almost every engagement, usually at the worst moment.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Each section takes one piece of that and shows it in use.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;► Package management, including installing .deb files.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;► Permissions, ownership, and octal notation.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;► Input and output streams in the shell.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;► Pipes, logical operators, and your own custom commands.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Filtering a large output down to the one line you need is a skill you use for the rest of your career.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;✅ Lifetime access to all modules and source files.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Get these three areas solid and the rest of Linux opens up.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h3 id="hands-onandroidhackinglabs_decompilingcodepatternsvulnerabilities"&gt;&lt;a id="hands-onandroidhackinglabs_decompilingcodepatternsvulnerabilities" href="https://youtu.be/hMwXlyC1qso"&gt;Hands-on Android Hacking Labs: Decompiling, Code Patterns, Vulnerabilities&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;img src="https://hb.imgix.net/ea6e0915f3f37fa0df8d70604fbdb88d752d093e.jpg?auto=compress,format&amp;fit=clip&amp;h=350&amp;w=600&amp;s=aad2e54b914cdb8235534deedc19c294"&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;Labs, not lectures. You decompile apps and read what is inside them.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;VulnDroid gets installed early so there is something intentionally broken to poke at.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;► Decompiling basics and recognizing code patterns.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;► Working with native libraries.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;► Installing VulnDroid and reading its logs.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;► Hardcoded secrets, shared preferences, files, and databases.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Most Android findings come from developers storing something where they should not have.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;✅ Lifetime access to all modules and source files.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Set up the lab and go looking.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h3 id="linuxfundamentalsforethicalhacking_thecompletejourney"&gt;&lt;a id="linuxfundamentalsforethicalhacking_thecompletejourney" href="https://youtu.be/hMwXlyC1qso"&gt;Linux Fundamentals for Ethical Hacking&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;img src="https://hb.imgix.net/1af6c0a42f763d16ac549fe18b2bf3ed71f1f490.jpg?auto=compress,format&amp;fit=clip&amp;h=350&amp;w=600&amp;s=2e4e76c51cd5ba5bfa5e7d9b28b8b708"&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;A short, practical start: get Kali running, then learn to move around it.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;4 lessons, no filler, aimed at someone who has never opened a terminal.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;► Installing Kali Linux on VirtualBox.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;► Reading man pages when you get stuck.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;► Creating, listing, and moving files and directories.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;► Hidden files and terminal based editors.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Nothing else in security makes sense until the file system stops feeling foreign.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;✅ Lifetime access to all modules and source files.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Install Kali and get your bearings.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h3 id="ethicalhackingandpenetrationtestingguide"&gt;&lt;a id="ethicalhackingandpenetrationtestingguide" href="https://youtu.be/hMwXlyC1qso"&gt;Ethical Hacking and Penetration Testing&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;img src="https://hb.imgix.net/149d28ddf1bd45da65fc7c489564dcc0863f2f92.jpg?auto=compress,format&amp;fit=clip&amp;h=350&amp;w=600&amp;s=a8db0eeecb239ed91ead410aae073217"&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;A full pass through an engagement, from first search to written findings.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Practical tips sit between the main sections, covering Shodan, Burp Suite, Metasploit, and WPA2 cracking.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;► Recon and OSINT before you touch anything.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;► Enumeration, scanning, and exploitation.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;► Post exploitation and data exfiltration.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;► Web application and API security.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;► Defense in depth, the dark web, and legal limits.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Testers who understand the defender's side write reports that actually get acted on.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;✅ Lifetime access to all modules and source files.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Follow the whole methodology start to finish.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h3 id="advancedandroidhacking_deepdiveintofridareverseengineeringandappma"&gt;&lt;a id="advancedandroidhacking_deepdiveintofridareverseengineeringandappma" href="https://youtu.be/hMwXlyC1qso"&gt;Advanced Android Hacking: Deep Dive into Frida, Reverse Engineering, and App Manipulation&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;img src="https://hb.imgix.net/5ffa67c2cc55adbe5c45f5a8b677fc95cc50d745.jpg?auto=compress,format&amp;fit=clip&amp;h=350&amp;w=600&amp;s=ef95a4aa59d2268a79f7762cf7d98dcf"&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;Frida lets you change what an app does while it is running, which is where static analysis runs out.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Short and focused, ending on a real ransomware sample.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;► The Frida framework and dynamic instrumentation.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;► Hooking into functions in a live app.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;► Starting apps from the command line.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;► Reverse engineering Android ransomware.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Watching an app leak its own secrets at runtime teaches more than any diagram.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;✅ Lifetime access to all modules and source files.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Attach to a process and see what it tells you.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h3 id="microsoftpowershellfundamentalswithazureft10practiceexams"&gt;&lt;a id="microsoftpowershellfundamentalswithazureft10practiceexams" href="https://youtu.be/hMwXlyC1qso"&gt;Microsoft PowerShell Fundamentals with Azure ft 10 Practice Exams&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;img src="https://hb.imgix.net/6c81b92dd5cff283fffe571e731a5bf02d4ce946.jpg?auto=compress,format&amp;fit=clip&amp;h=350&amp;w=600&amp;s=4c833edf36d96d7ee4f47fef33e2d94d"&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;PowerShell is how Windows and Azure administration gets automated instead of clicked.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The sections build from syntax up to writing your own functions.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;► Syntax, cmdlets, aliases, and command logs.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;► Pipes and output formatting.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;► Execution policy and PowerShell drives.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;► User profiles, functions, and modules.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Once the pipeline clicks, tasks that took an afternoon become a saved script.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;✅ Lifetime access to all modules and source files.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;✅ Practice exam with unlimited attempts.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Learn PowerShell properly and stop repeating yourself.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h3 id="automatingdatabaseworkflowswithn8nandsqlfirst-timeexclusivehumbleb"&gt;&lt;a id="automatingdatabaseworkflowswithn8nandsqlfirst-timeexclusivehumbleb" href="https://youtu.be/hMwXlyC1qso"&gt;Automating Database Workflows with n8n &amp; SQL&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;img src="https://hb.imgix.net/b19deebf905ea214cdd5f721ccace7b96db5daeb.jpg?auto=compress,format&amp;fit=clip&amp;h=350&amp;w=600&amp;s=36f7efae0120695f240db75b2c749280"&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;n8n handles the plumbing so your data lands in the right table without manual copying.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Every section builds a working flow, starting with the database connection.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;► Connecting PostgreSQL and Supabase to n8n.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;► Inserting sales data into your tables.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;► Capturing form submissions and visualizing them.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;► Importing data, running calculations, exporting to Google Sheets.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Automations like these quietly remove the most tedious part of working with data.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;✅ Lifetime access to all modules and source files.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Wire up your first workflow tonight.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h3 id="webapplicationsecurity"&gt;&lt;a id="webapplicationsecurity" href="https://youtu.be/hMwXlyC1qso"&gt;Web Application Security&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;img src="https://hb.imgix.net/a6ea3b59f5d1b01148f866d4a4bea75ce61d0247.jpg?auto=compress,format&amp;fit=clip&amp;h=350&amp;w=600&amp;s=8e37aea701dad012e92581eb4560d248"&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;Web apps get attacked constantly, and most of the successful attempts use well known techniques.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Each section pairs the attack with what stops it.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;► Web application architecture and common vulnerabilities.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;► Credential stuffing and password spraying.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;► Evilginx man in the middle attacks and mitigation.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;► Clickjacking, memory scraping, and wallet security.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;► Mitigation strategies and security tooling.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Knowing how an attack works is what makes the defense specific rather than generic.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;✅ Lifetime access to all modules and source files.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;See both sides of the same attack.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h3 id="pyspark_builddataframeswithpythonapachesparkandsql"&gt;&lt;a id="pyspark_builddataframeswithpythonapachesparkandsql" href="https://youtu.be/hMwXlyC1qso"&gt;PySpark - Build Dataframes with Python, Apache, Spark and SQL&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;img src="https://hb.imgix.net/83e8ceed0a613acc8e4b2645fc1ab846bf5decc0.jpg?auto=compress,format&amp;fit=clip&amp;h=350&amp;w=600&amp;s=b884d842c716fbd69bc9067552067073"&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;Pandas stops being enough at a certain data size, and Spark is the usual next step.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;You start a session early and stay hands on from there.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;► What Spark and resilient distributed datasets do.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;► Starting a session and loading CSV data.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;► DataFrame operations, formatting, and math.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;► Queries in PySpark and in Spark SQL.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Writing SQL against a Spark DataFrame is often the fastest way to answer a question about large data.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;✅ Lifetime access to all modules and source files.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Load your first dataset and query it.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h3 id="dataprotectionandencryption"&gt;&lt;a id="dataprotectionandencryption" href="https://youtu.be/hMwXlyC1qso"&gt;Data Protection and Encryption&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;img src="https://hb.imgix.net/8f8ef4e8a9bb3c2d6f25fdcdba2a0e7027a1330f.jpg?auto=compress,format&amp;fit=clip&amp;h=350&amp;w=600&amp;s=e4702a6123c804eca8b7a0ca0dbb61e6"&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;Encryption goes wrong in predictable ways, usually around keys rather than algorithms.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Concepts come first, then implementation, then the mistakes people keep making.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;► Which data needs protection, and HIPAA requirements.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;► Cryptography basics and encryption algorithms.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;► Key management and key rotation.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;► Encrypting databases and avoiding common errors.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;► Ransomware protection and complementary safeguards.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;An encrypted database with a badly stored key is not protected, and this shows why.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;✅ Lifetime access to all modules and source files.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Learn where encryption holds and where it breaks.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h3 id="pythonandsqlitebootcamp_learntobuilddatabases"&gt;&lt;a id="pythonandsqlitebootcamp_learntobuilddatabases" href="https://youtu.be/hMwXlyC1qso"&gt;Python and SQLite Bootcamp - Learn to Build Databases&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;img src="https://hb.imgix.net/ba7378af24cf0368c0d84cafb10f88b48593a519.jpg?auto=compress,format&amp;fit=clip&amp;h=350&amp;w=600&amp;s=0644b54abadaabc40727ce0d0ba9d01f"&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;SQLite needs no server, which makes it the easiest way to learn databases with Python.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;By the last section you are writing joins across your own tables.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;► Creating a database and building tables.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;► Inserting and selecting records.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;► Building rows from user input.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;► Checking for duplicates before writing.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;► SQL joins, from concept to working query.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Joins are where most beginners stall, so they get the space they need here.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;✅ Lifetime access to all modules and source files.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Build your first database from an empty file.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h3 id="linuxandunixcommandlinebasicsforbashzshellandubuntu"&gt;&lt;a id="linuxandunixcommandlinebasicsforbashzshellandubuntu" href="https://youtu.be/hMwXlyC1qso"&gt;Linux and Unix Command Line Basics for Bash, Z Shell and Ubuntu&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;img src="https://hb.imgix.net/89f40100ccecfcccda21c37de087713c499c407a.jpg?auto=compress,format&amp;fit=clip&amp;h=350&amp;w=600&amp;s=22d28cdc9d4f8ebc74e10758bad41679"&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;Straight forward lessons for anyone who has been avoiding the terminal.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Nothing assumed, nothing skipped.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;► Running your first command.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;► Navigating directories.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;► Creating and editing a file.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;► Moving files around.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Bash, Zsh, and Ubuntu all share these basics, so what you learn transfers.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;✅ Lifetime access to all modules and source files.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Type the first command and see how far it takes you.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h3 id="beginnersandroidhacking_practicallabsetupandtheoreticalfoundations"&gt;&lt;a id="beginnersandroidhacking_practicallabsetupandtheoreticalfoundations" href="https://youtu.be/hMwXlyC1qso"&gt;Beginners Android Hacking: Practical Lab Setup and Theoretical Foundations&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;img src="https://hb.imgix.net/99045d84e4a0aeb851ae3589c295275a110ff322.jpg?auto=compress,format&amp;fit=clip&amp;h=350&amp;w=600&amp;s=05af13cfcd604780dd04cdfbf2010b67"&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;Half the difficulty in Android work is getting the tooling to cooperate. That gets handled first.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Once the lab runs, you take an APK apart and put it back together.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;► Installing Java, decompilers, and Android Studio.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;► Setting up a rooted emulator and downloading APKs.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;► How an Android app is structured.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;► Decompiling, modifying, and recompiling an APK.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;► Running commands on the device and scripting the rebuild.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;A working lab is what turns Android security from reading into practice.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;✅ Lifetime access to all modules and source files.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Get the environment built and start pulling apps apart.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h3 id="pythonprogrammingfundamentalsvideoseries"&gt;&lt;a id="pythonprogrammingfundamentalsvideoseries" href="https://youtu.be/hMwXlyC1qso"&gt;Python Programming Fundamentals Video Series&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;img src="https://hb.imgix.net/8dc3c54f545395aeddb51a1e7ca85e9ac2dd49c6.jpg?auto=compress,format&amp;fit=clip&amp;h=350&amp;w=600&amp;s=fbfa946cbdcebf172638a40fd4a7710e"&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;Easy to follow lessons, each with worked examples rather than theory alone.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The sequence runs from variables to inheritance without gaps.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;► Variables, type conversion, and operators.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;► Lists, tuples, dictionaries, and ranges.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;► Conditionals and their variants.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;► While loops and for loops.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;► Functions, parameters, and return values.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;► Classes, objects, inheritance, and static members.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Every example gets its own section, so the concepts land before the next one arrives.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;✅ Lifetime access to all modules and source files.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Start at variables and work down the list.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h3 id="windowsterminalprofiles_customizationandefficiencyunleashed"&gt;&lt;a id="windowsterminalprofiles_customizationandefficiencyunleashed" href="https://youtu.be/hMwXlyC1qso"&gt;Windows Terminal Profiles: Customization and Efficiency Unleashed&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;img src="https://hb.imgix.net/87cce335a2a5bd3ae628496c92288505508b74a1.jpg?auto=compress,format&amp;fit=clip&amp;h=350&amp;w=600&amp;s=d7b5eb58fca9a6d6113e9769b56643b8"&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;Profiles are what let one terminal window handle PowerShell, WSL, and anything else you use.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Short and specific, all configuration work.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;► Creating and configuring profiles.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;► Font size and transparency settings.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;► Additional profile configuration.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;► Panes and a retro command prompt look.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;A terminal set up the way you work saves a few seconds hundreds of times a day.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;✅ Lifetime access to all modules and source files.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Configure yours and stop fighting the defaults.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h3 id="mobilesecurityvanguard-bestpracticesandstrategieswithpracticeexam"&gt;&lt;a id="mobilesecurityvanguard-bestpracticesandstrategieswithpracticeexam" href="https://youtu.be/hMwXlyC1qso"&gt;Mobile Security Vanguard - Best Practices and Strategies with Practice Exam&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;img src="https://hb.imgix.net/6f09ea7e07511467082ea13e584603d2536762ee.jpg?auto=compress,format&amp;fit=clip&amp;h=350&amp;w=600&amp;s=36177695d422c5a8e2afefe25eda23e1"&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;Phones hold more sensitive data than most laptops and get far less protection.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Sections alternate between concepts and specific mitigations.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;► Mobile platforms and current threats.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;► Securing devices, wifi, and Bluetooth.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;► Tapping, spoofing, camera and mic mitigation.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;► Data protection, privacy, and safe app use.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;► Mobile device management and incident response.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Locating a lost phone and blocking a spoofed device are both covered as tasks, not warnings.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;✅ Lifetime access to all modules and source files.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;✅ Practice exam with unlimited attempts.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Lock down the device in your pocket first.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h3 id="cloudsecurityandriskmanagement"&gt;&lt;a id="cloudsecurityandriskmanagement" href="https://youtu.be/hMwXlyC1qso"&gt;Cloud Security and Risk Management&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;img src="https://hb.imgix.net/4762f1f1c4e4a9c9118184c74aa456341a9c7318.jpg?auto=compress,format&amp;fit=clip&amp;h=350&amp;w=600&amp;s=940762c508502b37377918700c098a8b"&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;Shared responsibility means some of the security is yours, and that part is often left undone.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Threats come first, then controls, then how to assess and document risk.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;► Cloud security threats and insider risk.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;► Securing APIs and encrypting cloud data.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;► Risk assessment and policy drafting.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;► Case studies, including breach aftermath.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;► Security tooling and current practice.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Writing a cloud security policy is treated as a task you complete, not a topic you read about.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;✅ Lifetime access to all modules and source files.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Find out which half of the responsibility is yours.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h3 id="incidentresponseandthreathunting"&gt;&lt;a id="incidentresponseandthreathunting" href="https://youtu.be/hMwXlyC1qso"&gt;Incident Response and Threat Hunting&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;img src="https://hb.imgix.net/3871bd91a2153bb69c7ac69e8f3ec60667f635b4.jpg?auto=compress,format&amp;fit=clip&amp;h=350&amp;w=600&amp;s=245e3d181633b089caf55412145378dc"&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;Response is what you do after detection. Hunting is what you do to find what detection missed.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Both halves get covered, with documentation treated as part of the work.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;► The incident response lifecycle and IR plan.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;► Team roles and response documentation.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;► Malware eradication and rogue device hunting.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;► Threat intelligence and hunting techniques.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;► Hunting tools and SOAR workflows.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Teams that rehearse their plan recover faster than teams discovering gaps mid incident.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;✅ Lifetime access to all modules and source files.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Write the plan before you need it.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</description>
